	(footprint "local:USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-M-12"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "add2f849-a0d8-5785-bb58-535404191db9")
		(at 123.4 103.16 180)
		(descr "USB Type-C receptacle, HRO TYPE-C-31-M-12 (LCSC C165948). PROJECT FORK of the stock KiCad Connector_USB footprint, with two corrections from the measured STEP solder foot (out/j3-land/, 2026-07-20): (1) the SMT pad row moves 0.170mm toward the mouth (local y -4.045 -> -3.875) -- stock's IPC toe-extended land left only +0.080mm heel protrusion (below IPC-7351B Least 0.25, negative under the tolerance stack) while spending +0.520mm on toe; the shift gives heel +0.250 / toe +0.350 against the measured 0.850mm foot and covers 100% of the 0.200mm heel-fillet zone. (2) the two plastic-post NPTH holes go 0.65 -> 0.60mm, HRO's own drawing value -- this is what makes the shift legal, since the binding constraint is pad heel vs NPTH hole at the board's 0.25mm hole_clearance rule (0.60 gives exactly 0.250). It also halves the dominant tolerance term: the 0.500mm post now has 0.050mm radial slack. Pad sizes (0.6/0.3 x 1.45), x positions, pitch, shape, names, the shell slots, fab and courtyard are stock and UNCHANGED. The one silk change: the mouth-end cross-line is dropped and the two side verticals are clipped 3.9 -> 2.9, because a datum-correct placement overhangs the mouth 0.49mm past the board edge and stock's front-face silk would be plotted off the board (silk_edge_clearance). http://www.krhro.com/uploads/soft/180320/1-1P320120243.pdf")
		(tags "usb usb-c 2.0 pd")
		(property "Reference" "J3"
